      "body": "<!-- devin-review-comment {\"id\": \"BUG_pr-review-job-2043244f017d434a9144d5f621633950_0001\", \"file_path\": \"apps/web/app/components/canvas/CanvasBoard.tsx\", \"start_line\": 313, \"end_line\": 313, \"side\": \"RIGHT\", \"based_on_repo_rules\": false, \"kind\": \"bug\"} -->\n\n🔴 **Remote deletions remain on the canvas**\n\nWhen another user deletes a shape, `data.payload.id` throws because DELETE carries a null payload. The catch discards the operation, leaving the deleted shape visible until reload.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Learn more</summary>\n\nEvery remote operation carries `shapeId`, but DELETE operations carry a null payload. The server broadcasts that null value in [broadcast](https://github.com/sunnybagal/linea-seeded/blob/88fa083cae41d0e35652873c49fcb23d6e3ef151/apps/ws-backend/src/index.ts#L185-L193 \"apps/ws-backend/src/index.ts:185-193\"). Accessing `data.payload.id` throws inside the message handler's try block, so the catch silently skips the operation before it reaches [applyOp](https://github.com/sunnybagal/linea-seeded/blob/88fa083cae41d0e35652873c49fcb23d6e3ef151/apps/web/lib/canvas/canvas.ts#L457-L479 \"apps/web/lib/canvas/canvas.ts:457-479\"). The deleted shape remains in the live board even when it was not selected.\n\n**Example:** Alice and Bob see rectangle R. Bob deletes R; Alice receives `{\"opType\":\"DELETE\",\"shapeId\":\"R\",\"payload\":null}`. Alice's canvas still shows R until she reloads.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Compare `selectedIdRef.current` and `dragOrigShape?.id` with `op.shapeId`, which identifies the target for all operation types. Preserve the drag cancellation for matching operations.\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n          if (selectedIdRef.current === op.shapeId) {\n```\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/sunnybagal/linea-seeded/pull/1\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n\n---\n*Was this helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to provide feedback.*",
